[0.071, "o", "\r\n========================================================================\r\nACT 2 — The pipeline reads the code and catches it\r\n========================================================================\r\n"]
[0.036, "o", "Data files actually read by code/analysis.do (per GRAPH step):\r\n  - data/region_boost.csv  <-- NOT in README\r\n  - data/survey_data.csv\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\nContradiction(s) raised against the intake answers:\r\n  [intake_contradiction] You said this project does not use Stata, but I found `.do` files on disk. Is Stata required to reproduce any of the paper's outputs?\r\n\r\nAnd it doesn't just spot the undeclared file — it traces exactly\r\nwhich exhibit each data file feeds (the data availability statement,\r\nwritten automatically):\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  data/region_boost.csv  ->  tables/table1.tex  <-- undeclared in README\r\n  data/survey_data.csv  ->  tables/table1.tex\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n[press Enter to continue] "]
[33.774, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.107, "o", "\r\n========================================================================\r\nACT 3 — Full pipeline run, step by step (+ Docker)\r\n========================================================================\r\n\r\n--- DETECT --------------------------------------------------------------\r\n    author's intake answer checked first, then filename-only scan — before any file is opened\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "  restricted: False\r\n"]
[0.067, "o", "  working copy: /var/folders/5q/yhcyv3z55wvg6lhgc3h22kk00000gq/T/dr_os9qvgcz/toy_paper  (original project untouched)\r\n"]
[0.010, "o", "\r\n--- GRAPH ---------------------------------------------------------------\r\n    parse paper.tex + scripts into exhibits / data files / gaps\r\n  1 exhibit(s), 2 data file(s), 0 gap(s)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "  -> DATA-EXHIBIT-MAP.md written (data availability statement)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n  [DATA-EXHIBIT-MAP.md]"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n"]
[0.003, "o", "    # Data → Exhibit Map\r\n    \r\n    Which input data file(s) feed each paper exhibit, traced through\r\n    any intermediate processing scripts.\r\n    \r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "    | Exhibit | Data input(s) |\r\n    |---|---|\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "    | `tables/table1.tex` | `data/region_boost.csv`, `data/survey_data.csv` |\r\n"]
[0.355, "o", "\r\n--- CAPTURE -------------------------------------------------------------\r\n    infer language/packages/pin-method from lockfiles or static scan\r\n  language=Stata  confidence=0.30  packages=(none pinned)\r\n"]
[0.008, "o", "\r\n--- SCAN ----------------------------------------------------------------\r\n    extract external paths / package refs / secrets from every script\r\n  0 external path(s), 0 package ref(s)\r\n"]
[0.002, "o", "\r\n--- RESOLVE -------------------------------------------------------------\r\n    rewrite external/absolute paths to project-relative ones\r\n  0 path rewrite(s)\r\n"]
[0.002, "o", "\r\n--- ASK -----------------------------------------------------------------\r\n    surface gaps/contradictions that need the author, before spending compute\r\n  3 question(s) raised; author input required: False\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "\r\n--- FIX (deterministic) -------------------------------------------------\r\n    no-LLM fixes only, e.g. a script writing to the wrong output path\r\n  1 iteration(s), 0 fix(es) applied\r\n"]
[1.399, "o", "\r\n--- RUN (native) --------------------------------------------------------\r\n    actually execute the master script, unmodified sandbox aside\r\n  FAILED\r\n\r\n  stderr / log excerpt:\r\n    Stata error r(601) in log: /var/folders/5q/yhcyv3z55wvg6lhgc3h22kk00000gq/T/dr_os9qvgcz/toy_paper/analysis.log\r\n    \r\n    Log excerpt:\r\n    \r\n    . save \"`addon'\"\r\n    file /var/folders/5q/yhcyv3z55wvg6lhgc3h22kk00000gq/T//St72076.000001 saved\r\n        as .dta format\r\n    \r\n    . \r\n    . import delimited \"data/survey_data.csv\", clear\r\n    file data/survey_data.csv not found\r\n    r(601);\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n--- FIX (LLM) -----------------------------------------------------------\r\n    native run failed and no deterministic fix applies — hand the stderr + a directory listing to Claude\r\n  dispatching to Claude (live call)\r\n"]
[8.831, "o", "  1 iteration(s), converged=True\r\n\r\n  [model reasoning] [iter 0] The stderr clearly shows a file-not-found error: the script tries to load `data/survey_data.csv`, but the actual file on disk is `data/survey.csv`. I'll fix that path reference now.\r\n\r\n  -> applied: rewrite_path  code/analysis.do  data/survey_data.csv -> data/survey.csv\r\n"]
[1.284, "o", "\r\n  re-run after LLM fix: OK\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n--- VALIDATE (native) ---------------------------------------------------\r\n    check every exhibit the script claims to produce actually landed on disk\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "  present: [PosixPath('tables/table1.tex')]\r\n"]
[0.009, "o", "\r\n--- CLEAN ---------------------------------------------------------------\r\n    BFS from exhibits back through scripts to flag files nothing reaches (orphans)\r\n  2 orphan(s) — CLEANUP.md written\r\n\r\n--- DOCKER (GENERATE + BUILD + RUN, auto-fix loop) ----------------------\r\n    generate a Dockerfile, build it, run the master script inside, and if that fails, dispatch to Claude again — same fix loop, containerized\r\n  image tag: deadreckoning-toy_paper:latest\r\n"]
[2.584, "o", "\r\n  Dockerfile:\r\n    FROM --platform=linux/amd64 dataeditors/stata18_5-mp:2025-02-26\r\n    \r\n    WORKDIR /project\r\n    ENTRYPOINT []\r\n    CMD [\"bash\"]\r\n  build success: True\r\n  converged (build + run + validate): True\r\n"]
